{"description":"`bootstrap/discover.go` `detectGitRepo` walks from the target upward to the filesystem root with no bound. In any environment where a `.git` exists at or above the home directory (this one has `/home/m2codeloan/.git`), a scratch directory reports `IsGitRepo:true` with `GitRoot` pointing at the home directory. This breaks five tests in `eka-cli/bootstrap`: TestDiscoverEmptyDir, TestRunEmptyDirectory, TestRunExistingEkaRepoWithoutGit, TestRunStdinDevNullNonInteractive, TestRunStdinPipeNonInteractive. Interactive scaffolding is also wrong: `eka init` on a scratch directory believes a repository already exists.","impact":"CI red for any contributor whose home directory is a git repository - a common setup. Worse than the red suite is the silent misreport of repository state in normal use, which changes scaffolding behaviour. Fix: bound the walk at a documented boundary, or resolve through `git rev-parse --show-toplevel` semantics so the no-repository case is reported honestly. Add a regression test with a nested repository above the temporary target."}